From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:12:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] tests: add unit tests for the codec parsers and the
 media buffer allocator

A gst-check suite for libgstdroid that runs without Android: it defines
the droidmedia calls it needs itself, which take the place of the
libhybris glue built into libgstdroid. It is built with -Dtests=enabled
(needs gstreamer-check-1.0) and run with "meson test".

- hvcC codec_data of every size below the 23 bytes a record needs is
  refused, a complete one is taken.
- ADTS codec_data is made only from a frame with a whole ADTS header.
- ADTS frames shorter than their 7 or 9 byte header are refused, a
  header without payload gives no data, and an empty raw AAC frame too.
- The allocator gives GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_ENCODED for a HAL format it does
  not know, the right formats for known ones, and looks formats up from
  several threads at once.

Each input buffer holds exactly its own bytes, so that AddressSanitizer
or valgrind sees a read past it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
